A1. A dangerous place at which to meet a girl. ~ ALTAR
A5. A tower of Babble still in existence. ~ HAREM
A9. An archaic preposition. ~ UNTO
A10. A hero who gained high honors in the war. ~ ACE
A12. You must have a pull to do this. ~ DRAW
A14. This keeps many a thing under cover. ~ LID
A15. This may be easily put down, but it's apt to branch out into something big. ~ ACORN
A17. It's wrong to do this even in Paris. ~ ERR
A18. An abbreviation for Turkish Gunmen. ~ TG
A19. An Indian tribe. ~ UTE
A20. A poor fish often caught in X-word puzzles. ~ EEL
A22. One thing you must do to get anywhere. ~ GO
A23. A river famed for its beauty. ~ RHINE
A26. Implied—understood. ~ TACIT
A28. A tiny particle ~ ATOM
A29. Also. ~ TOO
A31. This comes with a horse's neck. ~ MANE
A32. The grand old lady. ~ DAME
A33. What the wolf at the door wants to do. ~ FEED
A34. This isn't much of an opening. ~ SLIT
A36. A supernatural being. ~ ELF
A38. For fear that. ~ LEST
A41. Many a dead one is in this place. ~ HADES
A43. Where many a sacrifice is made. ~ ALTAR
A44. A large chain store. (Abbr.) ~ AP
A45. This is always holding up things. ~ DAM
A47. Masculine name. ~ IRA
A48. Abbreviation for a Central State. ~ IA
A49. This usually lets you in on the ground floor. ~ KEY
A51. A watery silk fabric. ~ MOIRE
A53. A high priest and judge in Jewish history. ~ ELI
A54. Vivacity. ~ ELAN
A56. A prefix meaning upward. ~ AND
A57. A little bird ~ WREN
A58. Where they are always throwing the bull. ~ SPAIN
A59. A water-nymph. ~ NAIAD

D1. An indefinite article followed by something very dark. ~ ANIGHT
D2. Limited. (Abbr.) ~ LTD
D3. A preposition. ~ TO
D4. There's many a dashing young fellow in this. ~ RACE
D5. What few will be able to say "when the roll is called up yonder." ~ HERE
D6. A thoroughfare. (Abbr.) ~ RD
D7. Before. ~ ERE
D8. This is always on edge. ~ MARGIN
D9. Extreme. ~ ULTRA
D11. What most people work for. (Abbr.) ~ CO
D13. What 100,000 freshmen did last year for money. ~ WROTE
D15. What 100,000 chorus-girls did last year at night clubs. ~ ATE
D16. This has a catch in it. ~ NET
D19. What was Adam—before Eve came along? ~ UNMATED
D21. Thin layer of bone. ~ LAMELLA
D24. A binary compound of iodine. ~ IODID
D25. A river in Italy. ~ PO
D27. This fellow is learning the old army game. ~ CADET
D29. This is always holding a ball. ~ TEE
D30. Away from. ~ OFF
D34. What Gilda Gray would do to bring down the house. ~ SHAKE
D35. Blonde hairs on these have caused much trouble to married men. ~ LAPELS
D37. An exclamation. ~ LO
D39. What Columbus did to find America. ~ SAILED
D40. This has no legs but runs all over the country. ~ TRAIN
D42. Masculine name. ~ SAM
D43. Part of the verb "to be." ~ ARE
D46. A wailing cry ~ MOAN
D47. A metal ~ IRDN
D50. A doggy thing to do. ~ YAP
D52. Preposition. ~ IN
D53. A period of time. ~ ERA
D55. A continent. (Abbr.) ~ NA
D57. A group of islands in the Western Hemisphere. (Abbr.) ~ WI


Misprints, kept as printed (printed → meant):
A56: A prefix meaning upward. → ANO (printed key has AND; D47 'A metal' = IRON)

